{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And every woman shall ask of her neighbor.</b> Heaven forbid that the Holy One, blessed be He, should permit deceiving people's minds — that they should ask of them silver vessels and gold vessels and not return them. Rather, the expression ושאלה means that she shall give it to her as a gift, for so we find with Gideon (Judges 8:24): ״ויאמר אליהם גדעון אשאלה מכם שאלה ותתנו לי איש נזם שללו כי נזמי זהב להם כי ישמעאלים הם״, and so we find with Bathsheba (I Kings 2:20): ״שאלה אחת קטנה אנכי שואלת מאתך אל תמנע את אבישג השונמית״ — see, a gift that is called by the expression of שאלה. And what it says, 'a woman shall ask of her neighbor,' it should have said 'a man shall ask of the Egyptian'; but this is an a fortiori argument: if to the women they gave gifts, all the more so to the men; and similar to it (Isaiah 33:23): ״פסחים בזזו בז״ — a fortiori the swift ones. Thus wrote Rabbenu Hananel, of blessed memory."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Citation of I Kings 2:20 is given in the source as מלכים א ב׳:כ׳; the verse reference appears intact. The phrase אל תמנע is present in the biblical verse and supplied here; the source text in this comment appears truncated after השונמית, omitting it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:59.478968376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}